What is R-squared in Data Analysis?
R-squared (also written as R², or coefficient of determination) is a metric that tells you how well your regression model explains the variability of the target (dependent) variable.

R² = "How much of the change in Y is explained by X?"

R² = 1.0 → Perfect prediction
R² = 0.0 → Model explains none of the variance
R² < 0 → Model is worse than just predicting the mean

R2 = 1 -  (sum of squares of residual, errors)/(total sum of suqares, variance from the mean)

